{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-division-algorithm","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:division-algorithm","kind":"definition","title":"Division algorithm","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-admissible-system","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-remainder-module"],"tags":["groebner-basis","division","algorithm"],"leanRef":"ugb:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reduce","text":"division-algorithm.md","leanSource":"division-algorithm.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"def:division-algorithm\"></a>\n<strong>Definition.</strong> <em>Division algorithm</em></p>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> a commutative ring with unity, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-algebra\nwhich is free as an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module and without quasi-zeros, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(B, &#x3C;)</code> an\n<a href=\"#def:admissible-system\">admissible system</a> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>, a subset\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I \\subseteq A</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f \\in A</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde{f} \\in I</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r \\in O(I)</code> (the <em>remainder</em> of\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f</code> on <strong>division</strong> by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I</code>) so that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f = r + \\tilde{f}</code>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">i := 0</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f_0 := f</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>While</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f_i \\neq 0</code>:\n<ul>\n<li>Set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">i := i + 1</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>If</strong> there is no <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h \\in I</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{LT}(h) \\mid f</code>:\nset <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r_i := \\mathrm{LT}(f)</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f_i := f_{i-1} - r_i</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Else</strong>: choose <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h_i \\in I</code> with\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0 \\neq \\mathrm{LT}(h_i) \\mid f_{i-1}</code>; choose\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_i \\in R^*</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u_i, v_i \\in B</code> so that\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_i \\mathrm{LT}(u_i \\cdot h_i \\cdot v_i) = \\mathrm{LT}(f_{i-1})</code>;\nset <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f_i := f_{i-1} - \\lambda_i u_i \\cdot h_i \\cdot v_i</code> and\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r_i := 0</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Return <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r := \\sum_i r_i</code> and\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde{f} := \\sum_i \\lambda_i u_i \\cdot h_i \\cdot v_i = f - r</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Because we do not specify how to choose <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h_i</code> (nor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u_i, v_i</code>),\nthe output is not in general unique.</p>\n"}
